    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Jeremiah Shares Israel’s Misery"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I am the man who has seen misery",
          "Because of the rod of His wrath."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He has driven me and made me walk",
          "In darkness and not in light."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Indeed, He has turned His hand against me",
          "Repeatedly all the day."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He has consumed my flesh and my skin,",
          "He has broken my bones."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He has besieged and surrounded me with bitterness and hardship."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He has made me live in dark places,",
          "Like those who have long been dead."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          7
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He has walled me in so that I cannot go out;",
          "He has made my chain heavy."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          8
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Even when I cry out and call for help,",
          "He shuts out my prayer."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          9
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He has blocked my ways with cut stone;",
          "He has twisted my paths."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          10
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He is to me like a bear lying in wait,",
          "Like a lion in secret places."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          11
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He has made my ways deviate, and torn me to pieces;",
          "He has made me desolate."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          12
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He bent His bow",
          "And took aim at me as a target for the arrow."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          13
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He made the arrows of His quiver",
          "Enter my inward parts."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          14
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I have become a laughingstock to all my people,",
          "Their song of ridicule all the day."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          15
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He has filled me with bitterness,",
          "He has made me drink plenty of wormwood."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          16
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He has also made my teeth grind with gravel;",
          "He has made me cower in the dust."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          17
        ],
        "lines": [
          "My soul has been excluded from peace;",
          "I have forgotten happiness."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          18
        ],
        "lines": [
          "So I say, “My strength has failed,",
          "And so has my hope from the Lord.”"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Hope of Relief in God’s Mercy"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          19
        ],
        "lines": [
          "¶Remember my misery and my homelessness, the wormwood and bitterness."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          20
        ],
        "lines": [
          "My soul certainly remembers,",
          "And is bent over within me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          21
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I recall this to my mind,",
          "Therefore I wait."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          22
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The Lord’s acts of mercy indeed do not end,",
          "For His compassions do not fail."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          23
        ],
        "lines": [
          "They are new every morning;",
          "Great is Your faithfulness."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          24
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“The Lord is my portion,” says my soul,",
          "“Therefore I wait for Him.”"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          25
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The Lord is good to those who await Him,",
          "To the person who seeks Him."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          26
        ],
        "lines": [
          "It is good that he waits silently",
          "For the salvation of the Lord."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          27
        ],
        "lines": [
          "It is good for a man to bear",
          "The yoke in his youth."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          28
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Let him sit alone and keep quiet,",
          "Since He has laid it on him."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          29
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Let him put his mouth in the dust;",
          "Perhaps there is hope."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          30
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Let him give his cheek to the one who is going to strike him;",
          "Let him be filled with shame."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          31
        ],
        "lines": [
          "For the Lord will not reject forever,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          32
        ],
        "lines": [
          "For if He causes grief,",
          "Then He will have compassion",
          "In proportion to His abundant mercy."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          33
        ],
        "lines": [
          "For He does not afflict willingly",
          "Or grieve the sons of mankind."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          34
        ],
        "lines": [
          "To crush under one’s feet",
          "All the prisoners of the land,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          35
        ],
        "lines": [
          "To deprive a man of justice",
          "In the presence of the Most High,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          36
        ],
        "lines": [
          "To defraud someone in his lawsuit—",
          "Of these things the Lord does not approve."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          37
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Who is there who speaks and it comes to pass,",
          "Unless the Lord has commanded it?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          38
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Is it not from the mouth of the Most High",
          "That both adversity and good proceed?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          39
        ],
        "lines": [
          "¶Of what can any living mortal, or any man,",
          "Complain in view of his sins?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          40
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Let’s examine and search out our ways,",
          "And let’s return to the Lord."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          41
        ],
        "lines": [
          "We raise our heart and hands",
          "Toward God in heaven;"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          42
        ],
        "lines": [
          "We have done wrong and rebelled;",
          "You have not pardoned."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          43
        ],
        "lines": [
          "You have covered Yourself with anger",
          "And pursued us;",
          "You have slain and have not spared."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          44
        ],
        "lines": [
          "You have veiled Yourself with a cloud",
          "So that no prayer can pass through."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          45
        ],
        "lines": [
          "You have made us mere refuse and rubbish",
          "In the midst of the peoples."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          46
        ],
        "lines": [
          "All our enemies have opened their mouths against us."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          47
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Panic and pitfall have come upon us,",
          "Devastation and destruction;"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          48
        ],
        "lines": [
          "My eyes run down with streams of water",
          "Because of the destruction of the daughter of my people."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          49
        ],
        "lines": [
          "My eyes flow unceasingly,",
          "Without stopping,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          50
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Until the Lord looks down",
          "And sees from heaven."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          51
        ],
        "lines": [
          "My eyes bring pain to my soul",
          "Because of all the daughters of my city."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          52
        ],
        "lines": [
          "My enemies without reason",
          "Hunted me down like a bird;"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          53
        ],
        "lines": [
          "They have silenced me in the pit",
          "And have thrown stones on me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          54
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Waters flowed over my head;",
          "I said, “I am cut off!”"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          55
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I called on Your name, Lord,",
          "Out of the lowest pit."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          56
        ],
        "lines": [
          "You have heard my voice,",
          "“Do not cover Your ear from my plea for relief,",
          "From my cry for help.”"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          57
        ],
        "lines": [
          "You came near on the day I called to You;",
          "You said, “Do not fear!”"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          58
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Lord, You have pleaded my soul’s cause;",
          "You have redeemed my life."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          59
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Lord, You have seen my oppression;",
          "Judge my case."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          60
        ],
        "lines": [
          "You have seen all their vengeance,",
          "All their schemes against me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          61
        ],
        "lines": [
          "You have heard their reproach, Lord,",
          "All their schemes against me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          62
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The lips of my assailants and their talk",
          "Are against me all day long."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          63
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Look at their sitting and their rising;",
          "I am their mocking song."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          64
        ],
        "lines": [
          "You will repay them, Lord,",
          "In accordance with the work of their hands."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          65
        ],
        "lines": [
          "You will give them shamelessness of heart,",
          "Your curse will be on them."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          66
        ],
        "lines": [
          "You will pursue them in anger and eliminate them",
          "From under the heavens of the Lord!"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      }
    ]
  },
